{"t": 1792716630099, "cmd": "note", "args": ["--shot", "deaths", "First winter, day 1: three NPCs die of hunger (Fiona Robinson tick 195253, Nancy Williams 199797, Samantha Brown 200565). The top status toast just says 'Samantha Brown has died.' with no nation or cause; only the truncated chronicle line says she 'starved within the walls' of Castleford. No hunger warning preceded any death, and nothing on screen shows food or hunger for my own 15 residents, so I cannot tell whether my town is next or how to feed them."]}
{"t": 1792716630304, "cmd": "note", "args": ["--shot", "deaths", "Player energy never drains while standing inside the settlement (92.4 flat for 25,000+ ticks in winter), while outdoors winter roughly doubles drain (1 apple auto-eaten per ~2,000 ticks vs ~3,000 in autumn). Sheltering in town makes the player's winter trivial; the auto-eat also means the player never makes a food decision."]}
